@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [NewsletterSubscription]
+related:
+  - modules/newsletter/**
+  - guren.arch.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable-5-1/1.0", at: 2026-09-29T15:00:37.878Z }
+---
+
+# Newsletter sign-up lives in a self-contained module
+
+## Context
+
+Marketing wants a newsletter sign-up on the blog, and the same sign-up
+ships with the next product. Built into `app/` and `routes/`, it would
+have to be untangled from the blog before it could be reused.
+
+## Decision
+
+Everything newsletter-specific — routes, controller, validators, model
+and table definition — lives under `modules/newsletter/` and is loaded
+through `defineModule()`. The host application touches it in two places
+only, both written by `guren make:module`:
+
+- `src/app.ts` lists `newsletterModule` in `createApp({ modules })`.
+- `db/schema.ts` re-exports `modules/newsletter/db/schema.ts`, so
+  drizzle-kit generates the table's migration into `db/migrations/`
+  and `bun run db:migrate` applies it with the rest.
+
+`guren.arch.ts` makes `guren check` fail when a file under `app/` or
+`routes/` imports anything from `modules/newsletter/`, type-only
+imports included.
+
+Subscriptions are keyed by a lowercased email address. The confirmation
+token is 32 random bytes generated on the server; it is not fillable, so
+a request cannot choose it. Redirects back follow the `Referer` header
+only when it is same-origin, and fall back to `/` otherwise.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The folder can be copied into another Guren app, registered with
+  `guren make:module`-style wiring, and migrated there.
+- Blog features that want subscriber data cannot import the model; they
+  need an API the module exposes on purpose, and a change to the rule.
+- Unsubscribing takes only an email address, as requested, so anyone who
+  knows an address can remove it. A signed unsubscribe link belongs with
+  the confirmation-email ticket.
+- Confirming is a `GET` that writes, because the link is followed from
+  an email. Link scanners that prefetch URLs will confirm on the
+  reader's behalf.
